# Italian + English profanity, matched per whitespace token.
#
# Entries are run through normalise_for_match() at load, so accents, capitals,
# repeated letters and the usual character substitutions are handled for you:
# write the word once, the way it is spelled.
#
# Two rules were applied when cutting this list down, and both matter more than
# completeness:
#
#   1. Nothing that is ordinary exam vocabulary. "stupido", "idiota",
#      "cretino", "damn" and "hell" are all things a beginner reaches for
#      legitimately when describing a bad holiday, and masking them is a
#      pedagogical failure the README warns about.
#   2. Nothing that collapses onto a common word. The normaliser folds repeated
#      letters, so "ass" becomes "as" and would mask every "as" in an English
#      sentence. It is deliberately absent; "arse" and "asshole" cover it
#      without the collision. Two slurs were cut for the same reason and not a
#      softer one: "coon" collapses to "con", which is Italian for "with", and
#      "finocchio" is also fennel.

# --- Italian -----------------------------------------------------------------
cazzo
cazzata
cazzate
incazzato
incazzata
stronzo
stronza
stronzi
stronzata
stronzate
merda
merdoso
puttana
puttane
troia
troie
coglione
coglioni
vaffanculo
fanculo
culo
figa
fica
minchia
bastardo
bastarda
bastardi
sfigato
cagare
scoreggia
pompino
sborra
zoccola
frocio
negro
terrone

# --- English -----------------------------------------------------------------
fuck
fucks
fucking
fucked
fucker
motherfucker
shit
shite
shitty
bullshit
bitch
bitches
bastard
